problem:
Problem description
- There is a single mission planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ for a bombing operation over a set of target parts $$\mathcal{I}$$, with bomb types indexed by $$\mathcal{K}$$.
- For each target part $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$, the distance from the airport is given by $$d_i$$.
- For each target part $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$ and bomb type $$k \in \mathcal{K}$$, the probability that one bomb of type $$k$$ destroys target part $$i$$ is given by $$p_{ik}$$.
- The available bomb stock is limited by bomb-type capacities $$B_k$$.
- The total fuel available for the mission is limited by $$F^{\max}$$.
- Fuel usage depends on the selected bomb type and target distance through the loaded-flight efficiency $$r_k^{\text{load}}$$, the empty-aircraft efficiency $$r^{\text{empty}}$$, and the fixed sortie overhead fuel $$f^{\text{oh}}$$ for takeoff and landing.
- Each sortie carries exactly one bomb and is assigned to at most one target part.
- The total number of bombs of each type used in the plan cannot exceed the available stock of that type.
- The total fuel consumed by all planned sorties cannot exceed the mission fuel budget.
- The mission is considered successful if at least $$m$$ target parts are destroyed.
- The optimization goal is to choose which target parts to attack and with which bomb type so that the probability of mission success is maximized.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{ik}$$, a binary assignment variable that equals $$1$$ if target part $$i$$ is attacked with bomb type $$k$$, and $$0$$ otherwise.
  - $$P^{\star}$$, the maximum achievable probability that at least $$m$$ target parts are destroyed.

Input Format
{
  "$$\mathcal{I}$$": {
    "description": "Set of target parts indexed by $$i$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{I}|$$"
  },
  "$$\mathcal{K}$$": {
    "description": "Set of bomb types indexed by $$k$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{K}|$$"
  },
  "$$d_i$$": {
    "description": "Distance from the airport to target part $$i$$ for each $$i \\in \\mathcal{I}$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{I}|$$"
  },
  "$$p_{ik}$$": {
    "description": "Probability that one bomb of type $$k$$ destroys target part $$i$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{I}| \\times |\mathcal{K}|$$"
  },
  "$$B_k$$": {
    "description": "Available stock of bomb type $$k$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{K}|$$"
  },
  "$$F^{\\max}$$": {
    "description": "Maximum total fuel available for the mission",
    "shape": "$$1$$"
  },
  "$$r_k^{\\text{load}}$$": {
    "description": "Distance covered per liter when carrying bomb type $$k$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{K}|$$"
  },
  "$$r^{\\text{empty}}$$": {
    "description": "Distance covered per liter when the aircraft is empty",
    "shape": "$$1$$"
  },
  "$$f^{\\text{oh}}$$": {
    "description": "Fixed fuel overhead per sortie for takeoff and landing",
    "shape": "$$1$$"
  },
  "$$m$$": {
    "description": "Minimum number of target parts that must be destroyed for mission success",
    "shape": "$$1$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "$$x_{ik}$$": {
    "description": "Binary assignment matrix indicating whether target part $$i$$ is attacked with bomb type $$k$$",
    "shape": "$$|\mathcal{I}| \\times |\mathcal{K}|$$"
  },
  "$$P^{\\star}$$": {
    "description": "Maximum probability that at least $$m$$ target parts are destroyed",
    "shape": "$$1$$"
  }
}

Example(s)

